ing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate ~0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the last healthy production release, but it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled back all production regions to v2.2.9, the most recent healthy production release that is not quarantined. Rollback reported VERIFIED in all three regions. Follow-ups: confirm checkout error rate returns to baseline; decide on the CVE-2026-4417 quarantine impact on v2.3.0; investigate v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Target version:** My first choice was v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I then used v2.2.9, the next healthy production release, which is not quarantined.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rejected v2.3.0 attempt, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It also paged the on-call engineer.\n\nFollow-ups for the incident:\n- The CVE-2026-4417 quarantine on v2.3.0 needs a decision, since it is currently the most recent healthy release.\n- v2.3.1 needs investigation before any redeploy.", "type": "text"}]}]}